# Mixed Scripts and Unicode Coverage {#title}

This document exercises a wide range of Unicode scripts. NODX stores text as
UTF-8 and does not normalize identifiers; the AST preserves grapheme clusters,
combining marks, and ZWJ/ZWNJ sequences exactly as authored.

::::section {#scripts}
## Scripts Side by Side {#scripts-heading}

| Script | Sample | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Latin | Voix ambiguë d'un cœur qui au zéphyr préfère les jattes de kiwi | French, accented |
| Cyrillic | Съешь же ещё этих мягких французских булок | Russian pangram |
| Greek | Ξεσκεπάζω τὴν ψυχοφθόρα βδελυγμία | Greek pangram |
| Arabic | نص بالعربية مع أرقام ١٢٣ وأرقام ASCII 123 | RTL inside LTR row |
| Hebrew | דג סקרן שט בים מאוכזב ולפתע מצא חברה | RTL Hebrew pangram |
| Devanagari | ऋषियों को सताने वाले दुष्ट राक्षसों के राजा रावण | Hindi pangram |
| Thai | เป็นมนุษย์สุดประเสริฐเลิศคุณค่า | Thai with combining marks |
| Hiragana | あいうえおかきくけこ | Japanese hiragana |
| Hanzi | 中文支持是必须的 | Simplified Chinese |
| Hangul | 한국어 텍스트 | Korean |
| Emoji | 🎉 🚀 ✨ 👨‍👩‍👧‍👦 🇮🇹 | Including ZWJ family + flag |
:::: section

::::section {#bidi-mix}
## Bidi Embedded Examples {#bidi-mix-heading}

Inline RTL inside LTR paragraph: the value is [٩٨ ريال]{lang="ar" dir="rtl"}
charged to the customer.

:::quote {lang="he" dir="rtl"}
זוהי שורת ציטוט בעברית בתוך מסמך אנגלי.
::: quote

:::quote {lang="ru"}
Это цитата на русском языке внутри английского документа.
::: quote
:::: section

::::section {#combining}
## Combining Marks and Zero-Width Joiners {#combining-heading}

Decomposed: e + combining acute = é (NFC and NFD must round-trip).
Polytonic Greek: ἀρχή — breath + acute on alpha.
Vietnamese: Tiếng Việt với dấu thanh đầy đủ.
ZWJ emoji: 👨‍🚀 (man + ZWJ + rocket).
ZWNJ in Persian: می‌خواهم (mi + ZWNJ + xāham).

:::note {type="info"}
Per spec §6.2 NODX does **not** normalize Unicode. Identifiers and text are
compared byte-wise after UTF-8 decoding. Authors who need NFC SHOULD apply it
before authoring.
::: note
:::: section

::::section {#numerals}
## Numeral Systems

ASCII digits 0–9, Arabic-Indic ٠–٩, Eastern Arabic-Indic ۰–۹, Devanagari ०–९,
Bengali ০–৯. Identical semantics; rendering depends on font selection.
:::: section
